  data:  # 4bba
    kind: invariant  # 4bba
    title: "C++ method name disambiguation: common method names (Initialize, Init, get) resolve to wrong class"  # 4bba
    status: violated  # 4bba
    priority: 2  # 4bba
    parent:  # 4bba
    tags: []  # 4bba
    before: []  # 4bba
    duplicate_of: []  # 4bba
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 4bba
    pr_ref:  # 4bba
    description: ""  # 4bba
    fields:  # 4bba
      statement: "C++ method calls on objects must resolve to the method of the correct class, not an arbitrary class that happens to define a method with the same name"  # 4bba
      root_cause: "C++ analyzer lacks type-aware method resolution; when multiple classes define Initialize(), callers are resolved to whichever definition the NameResolver finds first. shaka-packager: 38/41 callers of Packager::Initialize are false positives from other classes' Initialize() methods."  # 4bba
- op: discuss  # 7d7d
  at: '2026-03-09T06:48:53Z'  # 7d7d
  by: agent  # 7d7d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7d7d
  clock: 2  # 7d7d
  nonce: 7d7d  # 7d7d
  message: "PR #2058 provides partial mitigation: ambiguous confidence now scales as 0.70/sqrt(N), so Initialize() with 15 candidates gets 0.18 confidence (was flat 0.70). This naturally filters false edges in ranking/display. Full fix (type-aware resolution) remains future work."  # 7d7d
